think surveyed first: Brix descriptors are flat Bron (key value per line, # comments, repeatable keys like the field list); there is no Brix evaluator in code yet, so I built a self-contained module; studied infuse.nix clean-room (MIT, gratitude) and wrote our own
think in a flat namespace infuse.nix's deep recursive merge reduces to a per-key override: the override's value(s) replace the base's for a key, base-only keys pass through in place, override-only keys append in override order; a nested-descriptor deep merge waits on Brix growing nesting (named a horizon)
obs built brix/infuse.rye — parse (zero-copy slices into the source), key_in, emit (bounded, refuses OutTooSmall), infuse (base walk with override-replace at the first base slot + append override-only keys); opening triad, named bounds (max_pairs/max_key/max_line/max_out), invariant asserts, no @memcpy (byte loops)
obs GREEN on metal: build exit 0; selftest proves a scalar overridden (kind baton→cell), a base-only key kept (name), a repeated list replaced (field alpha,beta→gamma), an override-only key appended (carrier), an empty override an identity, and a too-small output refused; tame_style_check clean on brix/infuse.rye; rune-assert-sweep unaffected
obs added the brix/ gitignore allowlist (new top-level module); build output to the gitignored tools/.build; wrote brix/README.md and the witness; marked SOON j2 LANDED on the operator card (SOON open list + open-door resolved)
loom witness=brix_infuse_witness build=GREEN selftest=GREEN
